Day 74 - Next Greater Element II

Problem Statement:
Given a circular integer array nums, return the next greater element for every element. If no greater element exists, return -1.

Code:

class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> nextGreaterElements(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        vector<int> ans(n);
        stack<int> s;

        for(int i = 2 * n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {

            while(!s.empty() && s.top() <= nums[i % n]) {
                s.pop();
            }

            if(s.empty()) {
                ans[i % n] = -1;
            }
            else {
                ans[i % n] = s.top();
            }

            s.push(nums[i % n]);
        }

        return ans;
    }
};





Time Complexity:
O(n), because each element is pushed and popped from the stack at most once.

Space Complexity:
O(n), for the stack and answer array.

Approach:
We use a monotonic decreasing stack and simulate the circular array by traversing 2*n elements.

i % n → maps the doubled traversal back to the original array.
stack → stores possible next greater elements.
Traverse from right to left.
Remove elements from the stack that are smaller than or equal to the current element.
If the stack is empty, the answer is -1.
Otherwise, the top of the stack is the next greater element.
Push the current element into the stack.

The 2*n traversal allows elements at the beginning of the array to find greater elements from the end of the array.

